# Django Social Profile Manager Roadmap

This plan summarizes the existing state of the Django-based Social Profile Manager and presents structured options for the next phase of development. 

The application is currently a fully-functional, beautifully-styled CRUD profile manager powered by Django, SQLite, and an Outfit/Plus Jakarta Sans glassmorphic custom CSS styling system. It includes robust data integrity validations, interactive statistics dashboard calculations, and secure CSV exporting.

---

## User Review Required

Please review the following structural aspects of the existing codebase:
> [!NOTE]
> The application currently uses SQLite for zero-configuration, beginner-friendly out-of-the-box local operation. Settings configuration files contain pre-commented schemas for transition to robust relational databases such as PostgreSQL or MySQL/MariaDB.
>
> If you are planning to deploy this application to production or a staging environment, we recommend migrating the database engine in the next phase.

---

## Open Questions

To tailor the next steps precisely to your learning or development goals, please review the proposed options below and let us know which features you would like to implement:

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Which enhancement do you want to prioritize first?**
>
> 1. **Option A: Dynamic Profile Search & Filtering**
>    - Add an elegant search bar in the dashboard to filter user profiles by username or age range in real-time.
> 2. **Option B: Dashboard Pagination**
>    - Incorporate standard Django pagination to cleanly slice long lists of profiles (e.g., 5 or 10 per page) with beautiful aesthetic navigation buttons.
> 3. **Option C: User Authentication & Profile Ownership**
>    - Link `UserProfile` entries to Django's built-in `User` model, ensuring users can only edit or delete their own profiles.
> 4. **Option D: RDBMS Database Migration (PostgreSQL / MySQL)**
>    - Migrate the backend storage from SQLite to PostgreSQL or MySQL, configuring environment variables for database credentials.

